[2026-03-08T16:45:01.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] • Yes. The biggest thing we had not borrowed from Aurora was not a specific color, it was its › Improve documentation in @filename   gpt-5.4 xhigh · 30% left · ~/Documents/GitHub/Aether
[2026-03-08T16:45:01.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   fallback strategy for unstable ChatGPT overlays.
[2026-03-08T16:45:01.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:45:01.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   The useful misses I still see are:
[2026-03-08T16:45:01.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:45:01.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   1. Dynamic overlay tagging.
[2026-03-08T16:45:02.805Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:45:02.805Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      Aurora’s glass.js does more than static CSS. It actively tags fast-changing UI like
[2026-03-08T16:45:02.805Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      [role="tooltip"], [role="alert"], [role="status"], search dialogs, and suggestion-list
[2026-03-08T16:45:02.805Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      wrappers with data-aurora-glass="true". Aether currently leans much more on static
[2026-03-08T16:45:02.805Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      selectors in styles.css and a little menu probing in content.js. That means Aurora is
[2026-03-08T16:45:02.805Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      more resilient when ChatGPT swaps wrapper classes.
[2026-03-08T16:45:02.870Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:45:02.870Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   2. Suggestion-list wrapper cleanup.
[2026-03-08T16:45:04.633Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:45:04.633Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      Aurora has a specific pass for ul[class*="divide-y"] wrappers in styles.css and tags
[2026-03-08T16:45:04.633Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      their parent shell. That is useful for search results, dropdown suggestions, and certain
[2026-03-08T16:45:04.633Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      picker menus. Aether covers generic menus and dialogs, but not that exact wrapper pattern
[2026-03-08T16:45:04.633Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      as aggressively.
[2026-03-08T16:45:04.633Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   3. Toast/status surfaces.
[2026-03-08T16:45:05.396Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:45:05.396Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      Aurora explicitly includes [role="alert"] and [role="status"] in its glass targets.
[2026-03-08T16:45:05.396Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      Aether does not currently style those, so transient notices can still pop in with native
[2026-03-08T16:45:05.396Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]      flat styling.
[2026-03-08T16:45:05.485Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:45:05.485Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:45:05.485Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   What we already captured from Aurora:
[2026-03-08T16:45:05.800Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:45:05.800Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:45:05.800Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - The tooltip/source-card pattern, which was the main citation miss.
[2026-03-08T16:45:06.275Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:45:06.275Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - The idea that the right surface is often a wrapper shell, not the obvious inner content.
[2026-03-08T16:45:06.768Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
