[2026-03-08T16:53:33.411Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:53:33.411Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   ## Summary
[2026-03-08T16:53:33.411Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:53:33.411Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   Aether is already strong in three areas: minimal permissions, local-only behavior, and a
[2026-03-08T16:53:33.411Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   clear visual identity driven by CSS tokens. The repo’s main weakness is concentration of
[2026-03-08T16:53:33.411Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   complexity: content.js, styles.css, and popup.js have each grown into multi-responsibility
[2026-03-08T16:53:33.411Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   control centers, which makes ChatGPT DOM churn, styling regressions, and popup/runtime
[2026-03-08T16:53:33.411Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   drift much more likely. The best improvement path is to stabilize the DOM contract first,
[2026-03-08T16:53:33.411Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   then modularize the popup/runtime around shared settings contracts, and finally tighten
[2026-03-08T16:53:33.411Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   test/tooling gates so regressions are caught before manual inspection.
[2026-03-08T16:53:34.410Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:53:34.410Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:53:34.410Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   ## Implementation Changes
[2026-03-08T16:53:34.410Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:53:34.410Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - Replace selector-chasing with a semantic surface contract.
[2026-03-08T16:53:35.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:53:35.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Add a DOM classification layer in the content script that assigns Aether-owned
[2026-03-08T16:53:35.401Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         attributes such as data-aether-surface and data-aether-glass.
[2026-03-08T16:53:38.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:53:38.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - First-class surface types should be fixed and explicit: tooltip, menu, dialog,
[2026-03-08T16:53:38.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         toast, search-panel, source-chip, activity-flyout, and research-viewer.
[2026-03-08T16:53:38.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Classification must rely on stable anchors only: ARIA roles, data-testid, and a
[2026-03-08T16:53:38.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         short curated selector registry. Avoid styling behavior that depends on raw
[2026-03-08T16:53:38.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         transient class fragments unless a specific anchor is known to be stable enough and
[2026-03-08T16:53:38.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         documented.
[2026-03-08T16:53:38.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Leave unknown overlays untouched rather than using speculative fallback styling.
[2026-03-08T16:53:38.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - Break content.js into small modules by concern.
[2026-03-08T16:53:38.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Extract at minimum: selector registry, surface tagging/classification, background/
[2026-03-08T16:53:38.407Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         media application, quick-settings UI, settings application, and observer wiring.
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Cut oversized functions such as quick-settings management, observer startup,
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         background image updates, research card tagging, and runtime cleanup into short
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         helpers with single responsibilities.
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Consolidate the two partial settings-application paths into one authoritative “apply
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         settings” pipeline with an explicit fast-path for tuning-only updates.
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Reduce full-subtree observer work by routing mutation handling through surface-
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         specific detectors instead of rerunning broad passes on every streamed update.
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - Convert injected CSS to surface-driven styling.
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Keep existing theme variables and visual language, but restyle dynamic overlays
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         through Aether-owned attributes instead of giant mixed selector sets.
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Collapse repeated deep-research/report selectors into one JS-tagged semantic surface
[2026-03-08T16:53:41.404Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         like data-aether-surface="research-viewer".
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Narrow the current glass “master selector” so it only targets stable layout roots
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         and Aether-tagged surfaces.
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Add brief comments above fragile selectors explaining the ChatGPT anchor they depend
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         on and what UI surface they are intended to control.
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - Introduce a shared settings schema/registry.
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Create one authoritative shared module that exports defaults, preset catalog,
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         bounds, sanitizers, and any popup-facing metadata.
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Make background.js the only source of truth for persisted settings semantics; popup
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         and content consume the shared schema instead of redefining bounds, fallback values,
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         or preset catalogs.
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Remove duplicated preset/default logic currently split across popup and shared
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         utils.
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Preserve existing storage keys unless a migration is explicitly required.
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - Restructure popup and background around explicit contracts.
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Split popup.js into focused modules such as state/bootstrap, tabs/search, custom
[2026-03-08T16:53:46.402Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         select, import/export, durability notices, and UI rendering.
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node] 
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Ensure render/update functions are side-effect free; sanitization and persistence
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         should happen in dedicated handlers, not during rendering.
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Replace popup open/closed styling driven by inline style inspection with semantic
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         classes or data-state.
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Refactor the background message handler from a long conditional ladder into a
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         dispatch map of small handlers.
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Wrap Chrome callback APIs with local promise helpers so error paths are explicit and
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         consistent.
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Keep service-worker startup simple and fail-fast; do not add extra loading modes or
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         hidden recovery paths.
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Fix small contract gaps such as missing data-i18n-aria-label application in the
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         popup.
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]   - Tighten tooling and repo hygiene.
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Exclude tmp/** from lint, format, and related repo scans so reference clones cannot
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]         break command surfaces.
[2026-03-08T16:53:50.403Z] [out] [id=2] [terminal=node]       - Add format:check to CI alongside lint and tests.
